            <ArticleTitle>Late bioprosthetic mitral valve thrombosis: a link with postoperative heparin-induced thrombocytopenia?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1310.e5-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.echo.2009.06.007</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bioprosthetic valve thrombosis is considered extremely unlikely, thus usually allowing patients to avoid long-term anticoagulation. The authors report the case of a patient with late bioprosthetic mitral valve thrombosis associated with a history of postoperative heparin-induced thrombocytopenia. The patient successfully underwent mitral valve replacement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
